Margin variant of R. Pinho's referee_check.py (not vendored here).

Upstream: https://github.com/rpinho/c86-trace-certificate, commit 116a58ff99681226ce6299d4a02eeff1e7d3c5c7,
file referee_check.py (sha256 8e30a480031338ccc68d028f138ad27d8b4e81d58409f89e77e4adc56d77ae1a).
That file is Copyright (c) 2026 Ricardo Pinho, MIT License (see LICENSE in that repository).

The patch changes only the E5 test: each bisection piece must have a certified lower bound
greater than MARGIN (default 1/10000000, override with the environment variable C86_MARGIN="p/q")
instead of greater than 0. ALL_OK True then certifies f >= 1/10000000 on the whole support.
Apply in a checkout of that commit with:  git apply /path/to/pinho_referee_check_margin.patch

--- a/referee_check.py
+++ b/referee_check.py
@@ -25,6 +25,8 @@
 import sympy as sp
 
 PREC = 128
+import os
+MARGIN = fmpq(*[int(v) for v in os.environ.get('C86_MARGIN', '1/10000000').split('/')])  # PATCH
 flint.ctx.prec = PREC
 X_ = sp.Symbol('x')
 
@@ -206,7 +208,7 @@
             fails.append(('budget exhausted', float(s), float(t)))
             break
         lb = lower_bound(s, t)
-        if lb > 0:
+        if lb > arb(MARGIN):   # PATCH: certify f >= MARGIN, not just f > 0
             n_ok += 1
             v = float(lb.lower())
             minlb = v if minlb is None else min(minlb, v)
